---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Md. Afnan is a student interested in technology, AI, research and web development, learning through the ongoing Nyayota project."
  path="/about/"
>
  <div class="container about-opening" data-hero>
    <div>
      <p class="folio-label" data-enter>About / Md. Afnan</p><h1
        data-title-line
      >
        A student.<br /><em>A work in progress.</em>
      </h1>
    </div>
    <p class="about-opening__note" data-enter>
      Technology, AI, research<br />&amp; web development.<br /><span
        >Exploring through projects.</span
      >
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="container personal-layout about-narrative">
    <div class="personal-reading">
      <section aria-labelledby="work-heading">
        <h2 id="work-heading">Hello, I’m Afnan.</h2><p class="reading-lead">
          I am a student with an interest in technology, AI, research and web
          development. I am still learning, and this site is a place to show the
          work as it develops.
        </p><p>
          What interests me is how useful information reaches someone: how it is
          organised, how it is explained, and whether an interface makes it
          easier to understand. Projects give those questions a concrete form
          while I develop my technical abilities.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="project-heading">
        <p class="folio-label">A project to think with</p><h2
          id="project-heading"
        >
          Why Nyayota is central here.
        </h2><p>
          <a href="/projects/nyayota/">Nyayota</a> is my main ongoing project. It
          brings Bangladeshi legal information into a browsable web interface. The
          subject makes questions about structure very concrete: an act has chapters
          and sections; a summary needs to remain distinguishable from a source;
          a reader needs to find their way back.
        </p><p>
          I use AI-assisted development. My involvement centres on the direction
          of the project, its requirements and how information is presented. The
          case study separates those decisions from the implementation visible
          in the repository. It does not claim that I independently wrote all
          the code.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/nyayota/#role"
          >Read about my contribution <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a
        >
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="interests-heading">
        <h2 id="interests-heading">What I want to understand better.</h2><dl
          class="interest-notes"
        >
          <div>
            <dt>Technology &amp; AI</dt><dd>
              How tools can help turn an idea into something useful, and where
              their output still needs checking. AI assistance is part of my
              workflow, not a substitute for understanding it.
            </dd>
          </div><div>
            <dt>Research &amp; sources</dt><dd>
              How to keep an explanation connected to its source. This is an
              interest in research and information, not a claim of published
              research or legal expertise.
            </dd>
          </div><div>
            <dt>Web development</dt><dd>
              How data, page structure, typography and interaction work
              together. I am developing my technical abilities while working on
              real interfaces.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section id="current-heading" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
        <h2 id="next-heading">The next part is learning.</h2><p>
          I want to better understand the systems I am working with: how
          structured data becomes a page, how to check AI-assisted changes, and
          how an interface behaves for someone using a phone or keyboard.
        </p><p>
          For now, the useful record is the ongoing project and its limitations.
          If I publish longer writing later, it will live on this site; it is
          not a publication record I have today.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/vault/#progress"
          >Read the learning notes <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a
        >
      </section>
    </div>
    <aside class="personal-margin" aria-label="A short introduction">
      <p class="folio-label">At the moment</p><p>{site.status}</p><dl
        class="plain-facts"
      >
        <div>
          <dt>Main project</dt><dd><a href="/projects/nyayota/">Nyayota</a></dd>
        </div><div><dt>Workflow</dt><dd>AI-assisted development</dd></div>
      </dl><a class="text-link" href="/cv/"
        >Project-focused CV <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={15} /></a
      ><a class="text-link" href="/contact/"
        >Get in touch <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={15} /></a
      >
    </aside>
  </div>
  <section class="container editorial-next">
    <p class="folio-label">An introduction through the work</p><h2>
      Start with Nyayota.<br /><em>Questions are welcome.</em>
    </h2><div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/projects/nyayota/"
        >Explore the project <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a
      ><a class="text-link" href="/contact/"
        >Contact me <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} /></a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
